{title: 479 - Tread Softly}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb]Be silent, be silent, A whisper [F]is [F7]heard,
[F7]Be silent, [Bb]and listen, [Eb]Oh, treasure [Bb]each word!
[Bb]Tread softly, [F/C]tread softly, [C7]The Master [F]is here,
[F7]Tread softly, [Bb]tread softly, [Eb]He bids us [F]draw [F7]near.

Refrain:
[F7]Tread softly, [Bb]tread softly, The [Eb]Master is here;
[Eb]Tread softly, [Bb]tread softly, [F]He [F7]bids us draw [Bb]near.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Be silent, be silent,
[F7]For [Bb]holy [Eb]this [Bb]place,
[Bb]This altar [C7]that echoes
[F7]The [Bb]message [Eb]of [F]grace.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Be silent, be silent,
[F7]Breathe [Bb]humbly [Eb]our [Bb]prayer;
[Bb]A foretaste [C7]of Eden
[F7]This [Bb]moment [Eb]we [F]share.

Verse 4:
[Bb]Be silent, be silent,
[F7]His [Bb]mercy [Eb]record;
[Bb]Be silent, [C7]be silent,
[F7]And [Bb]wait on [Eb]the [F]Lord.
